cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Shared Sky, please cite it as below."
title: "Shared Sky: a pre-registered simulation of delivery drones and air taxis over Houston and Dallas-Fort Worth"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: forgottenl5
version: 1.8.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24482589
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/forgottenl5/shared-sky"
url: "https://forgottenl5.github.io/shared-sky"
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered simulation of Wing, Zipline and Amazon delivery drones flying
  their FAA-filed operations over Houston and Dallas-Fort Worth. With realistic
  flights (corrected 26 Nov 2026), giving each company its own height cuts
  planned conflicts between companies by 61 % (Houston) and 72 % (Dallas-Fort
  Worth); with plans shared before take-off it cuts waiting for Wing and Zipline
  but not for Amazon. 86 registered studies; failed predictions are reported as
  failures.
keywords:
  - drones
  - delivery drones
  - airspace
  - UTM
  - simulation
  - pre-registration
